.TH CMX 1 2026-10-18 "cmx 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.\" Left-aligned and unhyphenated, so key names and paths copy as written.
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
cmx \- a minimal comic reader for .cbz files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmx
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B cmx \-\-thumbnail
.I SIZE INPUT OUTPUT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmx
(pronounced \(lqsee-mix\(rq) shows a comic one page at a time, or two side by side,
fit to the window, with nothing drawn over the image.
It opens each
.I FILE
in its own window.
Started with no
.IR FILE ,
it reopens the comic read last.
Every comic remembers its page, so opening it again resumes where you stopped.
.PP
A comic is a ZIP archive of images.
Pages are the archive's image files in natural order, so
.I page2.jpg
comes before
.IR page10.jpg .
When the archive has a
.IR ComicInfo.xml ,
its series, number and title make up the window title, and every field is shown
in the info panel.
RAR archives (.cbr), even when renamed to .cbz, are detected and not read.
.PP
cmx runs as a single instance: when it is already running, new windows open in
that process.
Opening a comic that is already open brings its window forward.
Comics can also be dropped onto a window.
Every window has the Wayland app_id
.BR io.github.DisposableSoftware.cmx ,
so compositor window rules can match it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-thumbnail " SIZE INPUT OUTPUT"
Write the first page of the comic
.I INPUT
to
.I OUTPUT
as a PNG of at most
.IR SIZE \(mu SIZE
pixels, and exit.
It exits with status 1, writing nothing, when
.I INPUT
can't be read.
This is what file managers run to show comic covers.
.PP
None of these options opens a window or contacts a running cmx.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Each binding has a name, used in the
.B [keybindings]
group of
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/keybindings.ini
(see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
To change one, write the name and a list of GTK accelerators separated by
.BR ; ,
for example
.BR "quit = <Ctrl>q;<Alt>F4" .
An empty value unbinds it.
.TP
.B open
Open comics.
Shows a file dialog; several comics can be chosen.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>o\fR
.TP
.B new\-window
New window.
Opens an empty window.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>n\fR
.TP
.B close\-window
Close window.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>w\fR
.TP
.B quit
Quit.
Closes every window.
.br
Keys: \fBq\fR, \fB<Ctrl>q\fR
.TP
.B next\-page
Next page.
Moves past every page on screen.
.br
Keys: \fBspace\fR, \fBRight\fR, \fBDown\fR, \fBPage_Down\fR, \fBl\fR, \fBj\fR
.TP
.B previous\-page
Previous page.
Moves back two pages in dual-page layout.
.br
Keys: \fB<Shift>space\fR, \fBLeft\fR, \fBUp\fR, \fBPage_Up\fR, \fBh\fR, \fBk\fR
.TP
.B first\-page
First page.
.br
Keys: \fBHome\fR
.TP
.B last\-page
Last page.
.br
Keys: \fBEnd\fR
.TP
.B toggle\-dual\-page
Toggle dual-page layout.
Shows the next page beside the current one.
A landscape page is always shown alone.
.br
Keys: \fBd\fR
.TP
.B toggle\-info
Toggle the info panel.
Shows the comic's metadata beside the page.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>i\fR
.TP
.B toggle\-fullscreen
Toggle fullscreen.
.br
Keys: \fBf\fR, \fBF11\fR
.TP
.B exit\-fullscreen
Leave fullscreen.
.br
Keys: \fBEscape\fR
.TP
.B about
About cmx.
.br
Keys: \fBF1\fR
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/config.ini
(usually
.IR ~/.config/cmx/config.ini )
when cmx starts; restart it to apply changes.
The file uses GLib key-file (INI) syntax and every key is optional.
.PP
When
.I config.ini
or
.I keybindings.ini
is missing, cmx creates it on start, listing every setting or binding at
its default but commented out: remove the leading
.B #
from a line and edit it.
A file that already exists is never written to, even when it is a symlink.
The same examples, with the values live, are installed as
.I share/doc/cmx/config.example.ini
and
.IR share/doc/cmx/keybindings.example.ini .
.SS [window]
.TP
.B width
The starting width of new windows in logical pixels, 300 to 8192.
When a comic opens, the window fits itself to the page.
.br
Default: \fB800\fR
.TP
.B height
The starting height of new windows in logical pixels, 200 to 8192.
.br
Default: \fB1000\fR
.SS [appearance]
.TP
.B flavor
The colour scheme, a Catppuccin flavor:
.BR latte ,
.BR frappe ,
.B macchiato
or
.BR mocha ,
or
.B gtk
to follow the GTK theme: its window background and text colours, the shades between
them mixed in Catppuccin's proportions, and its accent colour.
An unknown flavor is warned about and falls back to mocha.
.br
Default: \fBmocha\fR
.TP
.B accent
The Catppuccin accent colour, used for selection and focus:
rosewater, flamingo, pink, mauve, red, maroon, peach, yellow, green, teal, sky,
sapphire, blue or lavender.
An unknown accent is warned about and falls back to mauve.
Ignored when
.B flavor
is
.BR gtk .
.br
Default: \fBmauve\fR
.TP
.B opacity
The opacity of the window background, from 0.0 to 1.0, so the compositor's
wallpaper or blur shows through.
The page area stays black.
.br
Default: \fB0.85\fR
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/config.ini
Settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/keybindings.ini
Key bindings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/style.css
Optional CSS loaded after cmx's own, which can use the palette names such as
\fB@base\fR, \fB@mauve\fR and \fB@accent\fR. Every rule should start with
\fBwindow.cmx\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cmx/state.ini
The page each comic was left at, and the comic read last.
Written by cmx; not meant for editing.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/recently\-used.xbel
Comics that opened are added to the recently used files, so file choosers
list them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings are read; default
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Where reading progress is kept; default
.IR ~/.local/state .
